{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented and pushed as Gerrit change 2553 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2553), from a worktree off origin/main.\n\nAC4 first, because it is the premise: all three copies agree at 17/17, confirmed rather than assumed — canonical _CONFIRM_SCOPE 17, EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE 17, docs/user-guide.md 17, and the three sets are equal. python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check exits 0 on the committed tree.\n\nAC1/AC2/AC3 verified by mutating the REAL documents, not just the helper. Adding a bogus verb to the user-guide sentence fails with \"user-guide.md (mutation confirmations) is out of sync ... stale/extra [teleport]\"; dropping claim from EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE fails with \"EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE (scripts/gen_cli_reference.py) ... missing [claim]\". Each names the document and the direction. The unit tests cover the same two directions per copy against the pure prose_verb_drift helper.\n\nAC5: the original MUTATION_VERBS dict-keys arm is retained verbatim and still fires first; a test removes a key and asserts the original ValueError, then restores it.\n\nOne design point the plan did not cover. If the passage is rewritten so the regex stops matching, a plain set comparison would still fail — an empty set differs from the canonical 17 — but it would report all 17 verbs as missing and send the reader after the verbs rather than after the parser that stopped working. So prose_mutation_verbs returns None for no-match and the message is \"could not locate the sentence ... the confirmable-verb list is no longer gated\". There is a test for that specific case.\n\nGates: make lint, make typecheck clean; 31 passed / 3 skipped in tests/unit -k \"cli_reference or mutation_verbs or editorial\"; 9 passed in the new file."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788402905963068001,"uuid":"b33154d5-83d1-4f14-bd70-2415f62f0b04"}